   (or drop in a new findings CSV) and regenerate.

   XENON_PARAM (NAME, VALUE, EVIDENCE, MEASURED, SOURCE)
     NAME      parameter; rs6000.h defines XENON_<NAME> = VALUE
     VALUE     integer cycles (or bytes / KB / a count) used by GCC
     EVIDENCE  XENON_EV_REPEATABLE, _REPEATABLE_NOISY, _SINGLE_RUN,
               _UNVERIFIED or _DERIVED (plan D5)
     MEASURED  the measured figure the value is rounded from
     SOURCE    where it comes from

   The latencies and issue cycles of the insn classes are also written into
   the generated region of xenon.md (define_insn_reservation and the
   xenon_issue attribute) from the same rows.  */

